1
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:02,680
Hello there!

2
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:16,550
Incoming!

3
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:24,257
Everyone okay? Hideous. Tied up.

4
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:26,997
Did you have to yank us
back with your creepy jeans?

5
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:27,910
My mistake.

6
00:00:27,993 --> 00:00:29,960
I assumed that you wanted to live.

7
00:00:30,580 --> 00:00:32,460
You're tougher than I thought.

8
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:34,557
Enough playing defense.

9
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:36,880
Our best bet is to attack all at once.

10
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:39,017
Yeah, let's start throwing fists.

11
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:40,159
My blade is ready.

12
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:41,490
Agreed?

13
00:00:41,573 --> 00:00:43,499
Hope you're hungry for some arrows.

14
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:47,250
Futile.

15
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:50,460
Go, boring strike!

16
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:55,317
You'll find it impossible to
destroy my barrier of darkness.

17
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:58,460
Not for the protag! What's that?

18
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:00,070
History.

19
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:03,797
It's technically the world's oldest vending
machine from way back in the B .C.'s.

20
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:06,420
Behold, the Egyptian holy water dispenser!

21
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:08,520
Knowledge is power!

22
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:12,580
That substance dissolved my barrier?

23
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:15,175
Huh, that worked better than expected.

24
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:16,697
Score one for the good guys.

25
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:18,160
Ah-ka-ka!

26
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:26,090
Lamas!

27
00:01:26,173 --> 00:01:29,120
Their own shadows, I betrayed them. What?

28
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:34,660
Dang, that's a new one.

29
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:36,820
But maybe I can free Lamas.

30
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,100
That did the trick! It worked!

31
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:43,520
I was chasing a hunch my
barrier would free her. Nice!

32
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:49,520
I knew you would be the last thorn
in my side magic item. Nay, Voxo.

33
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:51,020
Thank you very much.

34
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:52,680
What's my next move?

35
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:55,392
It's too risky to go and free the others.

36
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:58,840
The stage has finally been set.

37
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,336
I trust you know what I'm getting at.

38
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:05,120
You wanna fight one-on-one?

39
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:10,120
Voxo and the Dalvik Knight, let us
settle this battle once and for all.

40
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:12,457
We can do this. Together!

41
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:13,800
Hello there.

42
00:02:22,340 --> 00:02:24,640
Here goes nothing. Yes.

43
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:33,840
Open wide, jaws of soil.

44
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,940
Infernal water.

45
00:02:45,580 --> 00:02:47,740
We got guarded? Not good.

46
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,620
Mopko, drop the barrier.

47
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:51,134
Leave this jerk to me.

48
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:57,520
Keep fighting.

49
00:02:57,780 --> 00:03:00,133
Your vain efforts are most entertaining.

50
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:02,657
It's been a battle just to get in range.

51
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:03,880
What do we do now?

52
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,070
Hmm.

53
00:03:06,153 --> 00:03:07,308
Truth is, I've got an idea.

54
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:10,737
A certain function caught my eye
when I first got to this world,

55
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:12,761
but I wasn't ready to use it yet.

56
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:15,416
It's finally time to give it a whirl.

57
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:19,940
The function I speak of is
pretty pricey, but let's splurge.

58
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:22,800
It costs a billion points!

59
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,414
The Transform ability!

60
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:29,253
Good thing I'm loaded thanks to the
Sacred Tree Dungeon Master's treasure!

61
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:32,740
Huh? Boxxo?

62
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:45,570
Impossible!

63
00:03:45,820 --> 00:03:48,585
How could mere water cut
through my evil staff?

64
00:03:50,420 --> 00:03:52,080
It was really cool!

65
00:03:52,620 --> 00:03:54,040
It's nothing fancy!

66
00:03:54,260 --> 00:03:58,017
I just cranked up a power washer's
pressure and fully constricted the nozzle,

67
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:00,537
essentially turning into
my own water jet cutter!

68
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:03,796
This thing could even slice
through steel and diamond!

69
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:06,560
Try that again!

70
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:11,590
Madness!

71
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:14,780
It's water and you haven't
even changed your form!

72
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,588
You ain't seen nothing yet!

73
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:17,920
Form change!

74
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:31,780
But now, you'll keep neutralizing
my impregnable barrier! Behold!

75
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:33,757
Transform's first ability!

76
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:34,840
What?

77
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:37,177
You just spoke like a normal person!

78
00:04:37,260 --> 00:04:39,877
Surprise bonus that while
Transform is active,

79
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:43,980
I can gab away by combining
all my speech functions! Sweet!

80
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:46,277
But that's not why I
rope the bank on this.

81
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:48,595
As for Transform's real first ability,

82
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:51,884
it lets me combine my
various bending functions!

83
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:55,829
What's more, I can swap out the
contents of any of my goods!

84
00:04:58,780 --> 00:04:59,610
Epic!

85
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:04,497
Now I can add a power washer and a gasoline
nozzle to my tried-and-true base form.

86
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:06,680
I can also replace fizzies, H2O,

87
00:05:06,820 --> 00:05:10,467
and so on with holy water in my
bottled beverages and nozzles.

88
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:13,760
If I can't defend, I'll deflect.

89
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:18,240
Give up yet.

90
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:20,577
Aw, the big bad thinks he's hot stuff.

91
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:21,700
Smolens! Yeah?

92
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:24,080
Jump up, as high as you can.

93
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:26,760
So you want me to jump real high?

94
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:28,980
If you don't mind. You know what?

95
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:31,397
Being able to really
talk to you is awesome.

96
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:32,480
I like it!

97
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:38,940
Next up, form change!

98
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:42,480
Used vehicle vending machine.

99
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:46,200
Activating barrier and
trampling them with drugs.

100
00:05:46,740 --> 00:05:50,460
Checkmate, certified
pre-owned barrage. Sure is.

101
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:56,600
Also, they're loaded with holy water.

102
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:12,790
Dang.

103
00:06:16,020 --> 00:06:16,850
Bravo.

104
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:20,032
I apologize for not taking you seriously.

105
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:25,580
Conserving my power against you was a
foolish error that I will now correct.

106
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:28,940
Um, are you as scared as me?

107
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:30,477
Because I'm scared stupid.

108
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:31,700
Don't worry.

109
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:34,320
I swear, we'll win this.

110
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:35,980
Just believe in me.

111
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:37,780
You really sure?

112
00:06:45,060 --> 00:06:47,260
Silly me. It's you.

113
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:49,400
I believe in you.

114
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:51,060
And I always have.

115
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:52,670
Yay!

116
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:06,180
I'll crush those brave spirits of yours
and relish every last moment of it.

117
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:13,460
Get down!

118
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:28,877
You deployed several barriers to increase
the overall strength just as I did.

119
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:31,180
Darn Skippy, I stole your idea.

120
00:07:31,860 --> 00:07:34,360
But it's still not enough.

121
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:41,680
Lamas, keep your eye on the
enemy. Stay strong. Got it!

122
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,340
Welp, let's roll.

123
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:46,640
Netherlord, don't blink or you'll miss it.

124
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:49,720
This is Transform's second power!

125
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:17,030
BAKXO!

126
00:08:27,220 --> 00:08:28,620
BAKXO!

127
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:41,497
You would rely on illusions.

128
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:43,260
In your final hour.

129
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:53,057
Your desperate struggles were in vain.

130
00:08:53,140 --> 00:08:56,857
I'm finally rid of that magic
box! Now I can. Too bad?

131
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:59,300
Dad, it's not over yet! What?

132
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:03,480
Team Voxo's going strong!

133
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:05,600
The illusions have barriers?

134
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:08,200
No, they're the real deal!

135
00:09:08,740 --> 00:09:09,570
Surprise!

136
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:11,460
We're all Voxo, baby!

137
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:14,800
Yup, that's Transform's second ability!

138
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:19,256
I can transform goods into clones of
myself with the exact same powers!

139
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:20,210
Meaning,

140
00:09:20,293 --> 00:09:23,097
my consciousness resides in
each of these vending machines,

141
00:09:23,180 --> 00:09:24,617
so I'm them and they're me!

142
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:27,524
Shout-out to the Ice
Vending Machine's comeback.

143
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:29,230
Gotta admit,

144
00:09:29,313 --> 00:09:31,177
I was hoping Transform would let me change

145
00:09:31,260 --> 00:09:33,907
into a giant robot or
something equally teak.

146
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:37,377
Feels like it should have been
called Clone or Copy or something,

147
00:09:37,460 --> 00:09:41,320
but as a vending machine
superfan, I am not mad about it.

148
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:45,859
Netherlord, hope you're ready to
face off against a brigade of Voxos!

149
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:47,310
Horrifying!

150
00:09:47,393 --> 00:09:49,620
This can't be happening! Oh, wow!

151
00:09:49,820 --> 00:09:51,397
That's a whole lot of Voxo!

152
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:52,310
No kidding!

153
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:54,337
But don't forget, there's a timer on it.

154
00:09:54,420 --> 00:09:56,300
That pesky 30-minute limit.

155
00:09:56,540 --> 00:09:57,817
And there's another catch.

156
00:09:57,900 --> 00:10:01,797
When time runs out, I can't turn into
other vending machines for a full day.

157
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:05,540
I gotta know, what do you call
this strategy? Let me see.

158
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:09,200
I shall call it Vending
Machine Corner Dream World.

159
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:10,960
Has a nice ring to it.

160
00:10:13,140 --> 00:10:16,357
It's like a dream world for
vending machine enthusiasts.

161
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:18,397
A happy little corner of the world packed

162
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:21,186
with tons of beauteous
mechanical aspirations.

163
00:10:21,300 --> 00:10:23,157
Enjoy this fantasy to the fullest.

164
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:24,520
I know I will!

165
00:10:25,140 --> 00:10:29,017
Numbers 4 through 20, give him the
old cardboard and balloon combo!

166
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:33,100
The rest of me, prepare to fire
using power washer nozzles!

167
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:38,457
Wait a sec, we gotta do it up right
for the final boss battle, so...

168
00:10:38,540 --> 00:10:42,960
Numbers 21 through 24, time
to transform into jukeboxes!

169
00:10:53,240 --> 00:10:54,457
What's with the muses?

170
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:57,820
You can't have a final boss
battle without a sick BGM.

171
00:10:58,540 --> 00:11:00,300
B-G-M?

172
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:02,980
Hope you're thirsty, big boy!

173
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:11,480
I will not give in.

174
00:11:11,700 --> 00:11:16,347
I'll throw even more powerful, overthrow
the demon lord, and reclaim my throne.

175
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:20,293
Sounds like copium, the mad
props for your determination.

176
00:11:20,740 --> 00:11:23,060
Anywho, try this on for size.

177
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:25,500
Triple nozzles all around!

178
00:11:25,820 --> 00:11:28,560
Shooting quadroplets of holy water!

179
00:11:28,920 --> 00:11:30,680
How do you like me now?

180
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,200
Rest in pieces, nether dork!

181
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:41,220
He's one tough cookie!

182
00:11:41,420 --> 00:11:43,400
Oxo, you wretch!

183
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:45,880
What sort of fiend from hell are you?

184
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:48,040
I'm a vending machine!

185
00:11:48,780 --> 00:11:50,540
Tag in, aerial squad!

186
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:52,337
Number seven's first in line!

187
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:54,160
Gotta love leading with luck!

188
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:56,200
Now, form change!

189
00:11:58,520 --> 00:12:00,640
Install concrete slabs!

190
00:12:00,940 --> 00:12:02,140
Eat concrete!

191
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:07,560
Block those 10, 12, and 17!

192
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:10,040
In that order, form change!

193
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:28,760
I knew you could do it!

194
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:30,177
You're amazing, Voxo!

195
00:12:30,260 --> 00:12:32,378
I wouldn't plan the parade just yet!

196
00:12:36,780 --> 00:12:41,660
I could see defeat, Voxo,
but one day you will be mine!

197
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:44,177
No, leave until your butt's fully kicked!

198
00:12:44,260 --> 00:12:46,100
Go, Lamas! Hop on up!

199
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:48,130
Hoppin'!

200
00:12:48,740 --> 00:12:49,860
Form change!

201
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:53,420
Ha ha ha!

202
00:12:56,020 --> 00:12:57,080
Watch this!

203
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:05,840
We were this close to winning!

204
00:13:06,100 --> 00:13:08,394
Cracky timing for Transform to run out!

205
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:09,530
Hold on!

206
00:13:09,613 --> 00:13:11,477
We've still got ten seconds left!

207
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:13,377
These fizzy bottles are filled with gas!

208
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:15,200
Check out my cola thrusters!

209
00:13:15,460 --> 00:13:16,860
Do your thing, lobbets!

210
00:13:27,380 --> 00:13:29,440
Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah!

211
00:13:31,700 --> 00:13:32,530
Ah!

212
00:13:45,060 --> 00:13:46,900
Now it's over? Yes!

213
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:48,340
Good work!

214
00:13:48,960 --> 00:13:49,790
All right.

215
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,977
You're back to being
the strong silent type.

216
00:13:52,060 --> 00:13:52,890
Yes.

217
00:13:53,020 --> 00:13:56,138
One more second and our
goose would have been cooked.

218
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:59,197
Hey, Lama! Mr. Boxos!

219
00:13:59,280 --> 00:14:00,940
But you really did it!

220
00:14:01,780 --> 00:14:03,037
You're not hurt, are you?

221
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:04,537
You can still produce food?

222
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:05,450
Yes.

223
00:14:05,533 --> 00:14:06,757
Please forgive me, Master.

224
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:09,417
I wasn't able to lend
you my sword in battle.

225
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:10,337
Cool fight.

226
00:14:10,420 --> 00:14:11,957
It was fun to see him squirm.

227
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:13,720
It was an ocean of boxos.

228
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:19,057
Neat trick, although I wish we'd been
close enough to get a better look.

229
00:14:19,140 --> 00:14:20,917
The captain's family missed out.

230
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:23,080
I wish everyone could have seen it.

231
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:26,144
Every director and all
of our friends back home.

232
00:14:26,420 --> 00:14:29,067
Speaking of home, the
magic portal is busted.

233
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:32,097
I'm guessing the Netherlord
burned through too much mana.

234
00:14:32,180 --> 00:14:34,597
You mean we're stuck
here for a while longer?

235
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:36,680
Hold on, won't we starve to death?

236
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:39,557
I may have used a boatload
of points on Transform,

237
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:41,457
but I still have plenty of snacks left.

238
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:44,658
I could comfortably feed
those six for several years.

239
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:47,877
I wouldn't worry about things
like that with Boxo around.

240
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:48,790
True.

241
00:14:48,873 --> 00:14:50,417
We know Boxo will always have our backs.

242
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:51,460
He's the best.

243
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:53,897
Yeah, I love how he
keeps us from starving.

244
00:14:53,980 --> 00:14:54,810
Same here.

245
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:56,580
Boxo is the greatest.

246
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,360
Master Boxo, I'll follow you till I die.

247
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:01,287
Thanks for everything, Boxo.

248
00:15:01,380 --> 00:15:03,017
I know we'll always be together.

249
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:03,930
Thanks.

250
00:15:04,020 --> 00:15:07,314
You shouldn't be the one who's
saying that, silly Billy.

251
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:15,400
He's powerful.

252
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:17,602
Please, Master, tread carefully.

253
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:19,030
Nervous?

254
00:15:19,113 --> 00:15:19,957
It seems I scared you.

255
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:22,140
Sorry, I am the left.

256
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:25,880
No, I'm the one and only
demon lord, the Baus.

257
00:15:27,660 --> 00:15:29,300
In the letter.

258
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:31,460
Who's in what letter?

259
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:35,021
You must mean the one you
got from that field guy.

260
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:37,378
Yes, I'm certain you've heard of me.

261
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:39,172
So, the rumors are true.

262
00:15:39,380 --> 00:15:41,380
You're a sentient vending machine.

263
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:42,900
Takes me back.

264
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:44,040
Back where?

265
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:46,657
How do you know what a vending machine is?

266
00:15:46,740 --> 00:15:49,328
Maybe we have more in
common than I thought.

267
00:15:49,500 --> 00:15:52,618
That's real fascinating,
but what are you doing here?

268
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:55,397
Avenging the butt-kicking
of your former ally?

269
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:56,310
Hardly.

270
00:15:56,393 --> 00:15:58,417
I came to collect you
and take you back home.

271
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:01,757
It's my understanding that your
magical portal isn't functioning.

272
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:04,320
But if I'm not welcome here...

273
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:05,930
Please stay.

274
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:07,780
We need the help. Indeed.

275
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:10,160
An evil god rules over this world.

276
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:13,260
But I'll spare the details
while we are still here.

277
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:22,560
I'm pleased to see
you're all in one piece.

278
00:16:22,760 --> 00:16:24,231
Excellent work, everyone.

279
00:16:24,780 --> 00:16:26,920
I knew you'd pull it off, Voxo.

280
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:29,797
After everything that Netherlord
put my family through,

281
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:31,677
I wanted to be the one to stop him.

282
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:33,820
But I'm still grateful. Thank you.

283
00:16:33,980 --> 00:16:36,568
Now we can put this
awful chapter behind us.

284
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:38,090
Valiant fight.

285
00:16:38,260 --> 00:16:39,997
They appreciate everything you did.

286
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:42,037
My whole family shares the sentiment.

287
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:44,355
I can't believe it's finally finished.

288
00:16:44,620 --> 00:16:45,520
I'm grateful.

289
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:47,210
Woo!

290
00:16:47,293 --> 00:16:48,277
I'm so fired up!

291
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:50,157
Saving the world's a total rush.

292
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:51,537
I'm just mad it's over.

293
00:16:51,620 --> 00:16:54,757
Now we can pour our little hearts
into rebuilding from rubble.

294
00:16:54,840 --> 00:16:58,717
Although the past is filled with
sorrow, we can build a better tomorrow.

295
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:00,240
You did well.

296
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:02,380
You need a little break.

297
00:17:02,680 --> 00:17:05,817
I imagine you're exhausted
after all of that commotion.

298
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:08,457
Getting enough rest is
part of a hunter's job.

299
00:17:08,540 --> 00:17:10,100
Hard work demands leisure.

300
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:12,500
Shui, we were worried about you.

301
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:14,797
Thank goodness you're okay.

302
00:17:14,880 --> 00:17:16,840
Good work out there. Thanks!

303
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:18,420
It was pretty fun.

304
00:17:18,980 --> 00:17:21,577
All of us from the whole
Clearflow Lake Stratum

305
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:24,307
are supremely proud of
our mightiest hunters.

306
00:17:24,800 --> 00:17:27,037
And I'm sure that those of us who didn't

307
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:30,760
live to see this day are
smiling down upon us.

308
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:41,510
Howdy!

309
00:17:41,593 --> 00:17:42,577
How's it hangin'?

310
00:17:42,660 --> 00:17:43,560
Hello there!

311
00:17:46,660 --> 00:17:50,600
We lead some strange lives
for two Japanese dudes, Bear.

312
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:52,980
When you get back?

313
00:17:53,140 --> 00:17:55,199
Are you talking smack about my mom?

314
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:57,540
Kidding, but no idea what you said.

315
00:17:58,160 --> 00:18:00,100
Oh, that's wicked clever.

316
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:02,980
I haven't had a chat in Japanese in ages.

317
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:06,360
When did I get back?

318
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:08,240
A few miles ago.

319
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:11,004
He was with our displaced pals.

320
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:15,635
Together we'll rebuild where the old
dungeon used to be, brick by brick.

321
00:18:15,860 --> 00:18:19,560
Somehow we're already at the
fortified city in just two days.

322
00:18:19,980 --> 00:18:22,920
Oh, it's nice to see
you, Boxo. Hello there.

323
00:18:23,120 --> 00:18:25,657
We heard the good news about
you defeating the Netherlord.

324
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:27,622
I wouldn't expect anything less.

325
00:18:27,780 --> 00:18:30,877
When I'm back in business,
be sure to pay us a visit.

326
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:33,280
I'll show you a good time on the house.

327
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:34,580
Not cool!

328
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:36,097
How come there aren't any smooth,

329
00:18:36,180 --> 00:18:39,277
sexy ladies handing out good
times in my neck of the woods?

330
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:41,100
I'm jealous as hell!

331
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:42,440
Hello there.

332
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:45,760
So, what's next on the docket?

333
00:18:45,980 --> 00:18:47,017
Dungeon exploration.

334
00:18:47,100 --> 00:18:50,757
I'm guessing you mean the ones that
dole out a wish for clearing them?

335
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:53,428
There's a chance I could
go human again too.

336
00:18:53,780 --> 00:18:55,920
Assuming I even fit in a dungeon!

337
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:59,137
If I find one you can fit
in, I'll let you know.

338
00:18:59,220 --> 00:19:00,050
Sound good?

339
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:01,417
Make it so.

340
00:19:01,500 --> 00:19:04,780
Yet another reason to go out
and wonder some dungeons!

341
00:19:05,540 --> 00:19:09,952
If we're ever both human, I hope we
can make the time to share a nice meal.

342
00:19:10,220 --> 00:19:11,050
Totally.

343
00:19:11,133 --> 00:19:12,860
I'd be stoked if that happened.

344
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:16,100
Still, no complaints
about my agrarian life.

345
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:17,536
I feel the same way.

346
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:20,117
Life as a vending
machine isn't too shabby.

347
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:22,024
Did you two find a way to chat?

348
00:19:22,220 --> 00:19:23,180
Hello there.

349
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:24,920
I hate to interrupt,

350
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:28,297
but there's something I'd like
to discuss with Field in private.

351
00:19:28,380 --> 00:19:29,498
What sort of thing?

352
00:19:29,760 --> 00:19:32,437
Remember that nasty
little comment you made

353
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:34,932
when you saw Miss Shirley and the others?

354
00:19:35,120 --> 00:19:35,950
Nacho!

355
00:19:36,033 --> 00:19:37,958
I look forward to serving you again.

356
00:19:40,860 --> 00:19:43,400
The story's really over? Yes.

357
00:19:44,340 --> 00:19:50,280
Hey, Boxxo, mind if I tag along, you
know, to the other dungeons? Hello there.

358
00:19:50,920 --> 00:19:53,157
You promise that's what you really want?

359
00:19:53,240 --> 00:19:54,080
Hello there.

360
00:19:54,660 --> 00:19:56,360
I couldn't be happier.

361
00:19:56,900 --> 00:19:59,620
You can do so many amazing things now.

362
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:03,297
I was worried maybe you didn't
need me lugging you around anymore.

363
00:20:03,380 --> 00:20:04,360
Not a chance.

364
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:06,317
You know you're my best girl.

365
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:08,357
We're like two halves of a sandwich!

366
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:11,381
We've always been together,
and we always will be.

367
00:20:11,940 --> 00:20:12,770
Thanks!

368
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,294
I'm the one who should be thanking you.

369
00:20:17,700 --> 00:20:19,520
Oh, wow! I kissed you!

370
00:20:21,980 --> 00:20:23,660
So, um, Boxxo?

371
00:20:24,280 --> 00:20:28,045
There's something I've been meaning
to tell you for a while now.

372
00:20:29,140 --> 00:20:30,600
Okay, but just say it.

373
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:32,920
I've fallen in love. Boxxo!

374
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:38,240
Oh, hey, bad timing.

375
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:45,900
That didn't go the way
I imagined it would.

376
00:20:47,180 --> 00:20:48,140
For me?

377
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:51,400
Lamas, figs for everything.

378
00:20:52,020 --> 00:20:53,255
Here's to our future.

379
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:54,880
I love you.

380
00:20:59,840 --> 00:21:03,080
I love you too, Foxo, with my whole heart.

381
00:21:04,220 --> 00:21:05,617
Cheers to victory.

382
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:07,000
Cheers to that!

383
00:21:07,320 --> 00:21:08,920
We all worked so hard!

384
00:21:09,060 --> 00:21:10,457
Eat as much as you want!

385
00:21:10,540 --> 00:21:12,837
Everyone's welcome to
join the festivities!

386
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:14,920
This award is such an inspiration!

387
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:21,160
Say, ah!

388
00:21:21,880 --> 00:21:23,840
You're embarrassing me, big sis!

389
00:21:24,180 --> 00:21:25,180
Both and wide!

390
00:21:25,600 --> 00:21:28,129
How's our tiny bro a
certified lady killer?

391
00:21:28,260 --> 00:21:29,090
That tears it!

392
00:21:29,173 --> 00:21:31,017
Let's go hunting for girlfriends!

393
00:21:31,100 --> 00:21:32,480
My poor boys!

394
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:38,820
You look scrumptious,
truly Are you drunk, Lamy?

395
00:21:40,040 --> 00:21:42,477
You changed our lives, Foxhole.

396
00:21:42,560 --> 00:21:44,577
You sure look pretty.

397
00:21:44,660 --> 00:21:47,097
Tonight's been just perfect!

398
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:48,980
I'm glad we hung in there.

399
00:21:51,240 --> 00:21:52,757
It's a heck of a party?

400
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:53,820
Having fun?

401
00:21:54,060 --> 00:22:00,660
Yes I was reborn as a vending machine
In another world Not gonna lie,

402
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:01,897
it's a pretty ridiculous premise?

403
00:22:01,980 --> 00:22:05,160
But now, I'm surrounded
by people I care about.

404
00:22:05,340 --> 00:22:06,240
So who cares?

405
00:22:06,540 --> 00:22:08,360
I'm living my best life!

406
00:22:10,460 --> 00:22:12,931
You're saying a magic box saved the world?

407
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:15,300
I've never heard of a vending machine.

408
00:22:15,420 --> 00:22:16,479
I speak the truth.

409
00:22:16,740 --> 00:22:21,117
Not only could he dish out food and drinks,
but all sorts of everyday items, too.

410
00:22:21,200 --> 00:22:23,120
A refrigerated dream come true.

411
00:22:23,380 --> 00:22:26,637
A metal box with internal dialogue
that could change its shape?

412
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:29,277
Aw, Pops, I bet you're just
lying to us because we're kids.

413
00:22:29,360 --> 00:22:30,190
Big Brother!

414
00:22:30,500 --> 00:22:33,559
I'm thinking you should
call me Pal instead of Pops.

415
00:22:34,560 --> 00:22:36,100
Here, a little treat.

416
00:22:38,420 --> 00:22:39,440
That's the stuff?

417
00:22:39,640 --> 00:22:41,277
I've never had anything so tasty.

418
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:42,772
It makes my tummy happy.

419
00:22:43,080 --> 00:22:44,740
I'm glad. Pops?

420
00:22:44,860 --> 00:22:46,580
I mean, Pal? Question.

421
00:22:46,860 --> 00:22:48,389
Where did these come from?

422
00:22:48,960 --> 00:22:51,136
Let's just say I'm good at conjuring.

423
00:22:51,660 --> 00:22:52,490
Conjuring?

424
00:22:52,573 --> 00:22:54,537
It's sort of like magic. It's magic?

425
00:22:54,620 --> 00:22:56,117
I didn't know you knew magic.

426
00:22:56,200 --> 00:22:57,460
You gotta show me.

427
00:22:57,660 --> 00:22:59,277
Fine, if you insist.

428
00:22:59,360 --> 00:23:01,260
Ah, I found ya.

429
00:23:02,100 --> 00:23:04,097
It's time to go explore the dungeon.

430
00:23:04,180 --> 00:23:05,356
The gang's all here.

431
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:08,397
Somehow I'm still not used to that sight.

432
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:09,937
You know, I think he's cute.

433
00:23:10,020 --> 00:23:11,640
He's truly a man among men.

434
00:23:11,820 --> 00:23:14,037
I'm way too hungry to conquer a dungeon.

435
00:23:14,120 --> 00:23:16,414
I could use a fresh pair of boots, too.

436
00:23:16,600 --> 00:23:17,430
Right.

437
00:23:17,513 --> 00:23:19,417
My friends and I are off to the dungeon.

438
00:23:19,500 --> 00:23:22,480
But I'll show you one
last trick before we go.

439
00:23:25,820 --> 00:23:26,700
Hello there.

440
00:23:27,940 --> 00:23:29,540
I hope you get your wish.

441
00:23:29,740 --> 00:23:31,977
We'll keep wandering this
dungeon until you do.

442
00:23:32,060 --> 00:23:35,001
So if you're ready, then
just say the magic words.

443
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:36,180
Hello there!
